                <pb facs="0279" n="229" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav03/pg229"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.77/362</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Russia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Francis</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Vologda</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-04-09T20:00:00+02:31"><hi rendition="#italic">April 9, 1918,
                                8 p.m.</hi></date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received April 13, 5.43 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>84. Your 51, April 6, 6 p.m. I gave reasons for requesting railroad men in my 73,
                    April 5, 5 p.m., but as situation changed, better defer sending until relations
                    with Soviet government better defined.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Francis</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
